    <briefdescription>
<para>Error diagnostics needs to be equally usable in C and C++ code. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This is why there is a common infrastructure for errors.</para><para>Any error or warning or note is represented by an instance of struct error.</para><para>struct error has the most common members, but more importantly it has a type descriptor, which makes it possible to work with C++ exceptions and extra members via reflection, in pure C.</para><para>(destroy) is there to gracefully delete C++ exceptions from C. </para>    </detaileddescription>
